course: dictionary
lesson: 3485
title: Famous and what it tells you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Famous» means known by very many people. When a text says a singer is famous, you know lots of people have heard of her, even if you have not. «The famous singer waved to the crowd.» The crowd is there to see her, which is the clue.
explain: Look for the words after famous. «Paris is famous for the Eiffel Tower» tells you the reason it is known: the Eiffel Tower. So famous for means known because of something. Read the words that come next and they will often tell you why.
explain: Some phrases use famous in a special way. «World-famous» means known all over the world. «Famous last words» is a joke saying, used when someone is sure about something and is about to be proved wrong. Do not take it literally: it is a saying, not a list of words from a famous person.
fact: Famous means known by very many people.
fact: «Famous for» means known because of something, as in «famous for the Eiffel Tower».
fact: «World-famous» means known all over the world.
fact: «Famous last words» is a saying used when someone is sure, but is about to be wrong.
fact: A good check is to swap in «well known» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The famous singer waved to the crowd.» What does famous mean here? | Very tired after a long show | *Known by very many people | Standing very still | Wearing lots of jewellery
exercise: «Paris is famous for the Eiffel Tower.» What does famous for mean? | Afraid of tall towers | *Known because of the Eiffel Tower | Painted in bright colours | Built by the French last week
exercise: Which word means known by very many people? | *famous | hidden | empty | quiet
test: «Ella wanted to be a famous explorer one day.» What does famous tell you about the explorer? | She is afraid of the sea | She sails on a boat | She is very small | *Many people would know her name
test: What does «famous last words» mean as a saying? | The last words of a famous actor in a film | Words written in gold | A poem read at a funeral | *A saying used when someone is sure but is about to be proved wrong
exam: «Beowulf is a famous poem.» What does famous mean in this sentence? | Written in very old English | Long and very boring | Easy to read aloud | *Known by very many people
